**Read:** [Gases and Applications — Linde](../sources/Gases-and-Applications-Linde.lingua#r_72580QNZ60FMQAARB8ZG7SRTFT), neon, krypton and xenon entries; the cryogenic separation readings and primary sources behind any chosen recovery process.

A useful gas may occur at low concentration in a large source stream. Production then depends on concentrating an intermediate, purifying it and coordinating with the main plant's operation. A small product mass does not imply a small infrastructure requirement. Trace impurities become a different separation problem after concentration.

Distinguish abundance, technically recoverable amount, actual recovered output and delivered service. Product demand, storage, analysis and recovery from users affect supply. Historical market quantities and process examples retain their dates; the physical account should expose the assumptions needed to update them.

**Work:** Trace a selected rare gas from its source through concentration, purification and a defined application. Close an order-of-magnitude constituent balance using cited composition and recovery data. Compare primary production with a plausible recovery-from-use route, identifying the evidence missing before claiming equivalent purity or cost.

